      "description": "Watch Levski Sofia vs Kairat Almaty highlights and goals from UEFA Champions League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 4, 2026. The stage was set for a high-stakes UEFA Champions League encounter on August 4, 2026 . Both Levski Sofia and Kairat Almaty entered the pitch with everything to play for, creating an atmosphere of intense anticipation among the supporters. Tactical Stalemate and Substitutions The match began with a cautious approach from both sides, as the first half saw a disciplined defensive display that left clear-cut chances at a premium. As the second half got underway, Levski Sofia looked to break the deadlock by introducing Mazire Soula in place of Nikola Serafimov . The tactical battle intensified as the hour mark passed, with Kairat Almaty responding by bringing on Ismail Bekbolat and Damir Kasabulat to maintain their energy levels. As the game entered its final stages, the managers utilized their benches extensively. A triple substitution for Kairat Almaty in the 78th minute saw the introduction of Juan Perea , Erkin Tapalov , and Mansur Birkurmanov . Meanwhile, Levski Sofia made their final tactical adjustment in the 90th minute, bringing on Stivan Stoyanchov for Everton Bala , signaling a desperate final push for a result. Stoppage Time Drama Just as it appeared the points would be shared, the breakthrough arrived in spectacular fashion. In the second minute of added time, Sergio Araujo produced a moment of magic to find the back of the net, sending the home crowd into raptures. The emotional high was evident as Araujo received a yellow card for his celebration shortly after. Despite the late pressure, the referee’s whistle at 90+6' confirmed a hard-fought victory for the Bulgarian side, capping off a night of pure footballing drama."
